store-archived-sessions-under-sessions

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: store-archived-sessions-under-sessions

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Store archived sessions under CODEX_HOME/sessions/archives instead of a separate archived_sessions root.

Requires: Unit:backend/rebuild-sqlite-history-from-paginated-rollouts, Unit:backend/backup-sessions-with-native-locks

Provides: Use the nested archive path for archive, restore, lookup, search, metadata backfill and history reconstruction; keep active and archived traversal disjoint, preserve active precedence, and back up and measure each file once.

Boundary: No old-path compatibility, existing-file relocation or SQLite migration; preserve native writer ownership, archive rollback, compression, retained history and ordinary session lifecycle. The user owns existing SQLite deletion and rebuilding.

Verification: Focused archive and restore, active lookup, plain and compressed search, index precedence, database reconstruction, exact backup members, doctor inventory and separate storage totals.


